# `size(&text)` and `size(&a)`, `size(&b)` make cold frames that only an
# await in the same body takes, `f!()` or `join!`, so the locals they
# refer to outlive them (#1355): the `Ref`s are `lent`, each local drops
# after the await, and the call builds the frame through `size.lent`,
# which takes no count of the referent. The frames `race!` takes go into
# a list and keep the counting constructor.
